!! Forks I ruled in-house (each overrulable; the-veil-ladder carries 9)
* Ruling 9: a joined face's first bind also binds the place tree with the same route. Without it the landing's `secret-home` row refused `no-custody-slot` (smoke tw3), since a joiner bound a face tree only.
* A herm reads by the operator's ask (`--recipe herm` → `askedHerm`), since every faceless node place composes as "herm"; an asked herm derives no floor key even with its custody open.
* The node's floor key stands wherever the custody stands open, whatever rows the composition was handed (one reading with the control document). A first cut read `sovereign: null` as `vessel-locked`; CI e2e session-sign-reach S2 refused on it (the host working binding met `floor-unavailable: vessel-locked` on a founded node composed at its floor over an open custody), so that rule left. S2 was NOT rerun locally (an e2e file).
* The founding door carries its ask in sessionStorage across one reload (the admit landing's precedent), never a vessel verb.
* A control row `daemon-slot/<kind>/floor` files nothing now (no back-compat).

